  "chapter": "Events",
  "title": "Your feed",
  "brief": "People open their feed far more often than they post: 120 feed reads and 5 posts arrive each second. A user follows 20 accounts, so building the feed when it is read (fan-out on read) means 20 reads for every feed: 2,400 reads a second, more than any database tier. Build it when posts are written instead (fan-out on write): a Worker for the Feed Subscription writes each post into the feed of every follower, 30 writes per post, and reading a feed becomes one read.",
